  "description": "The Independent Science Society undersigns Science Works\u2019 Letter On UKRI Eligibility Rules",
  "body_html": "<p>Right now, it\u2019s almost impossible for new organisations to be eligible for funding from UK Research and Innovation (UKRI). UKRI is one of the main bodies that award money to science research. You basically need to be part of a University or huge org to ask for a grant.</p><p>But we should allow for the option for science to be done <strong>outside</strong> of universities. The Independent Science Society believes that this yields<a href=\"https://chillphysicsenjoyer.substack.com/p/why-independent-science-now?utm_source=publication-search\"> high risk-reward discovery, has convincing historical precedent, and increases empirical skills amongst the public.</a> That\u2019s what this whole blog is trying to prove. But don\u2019t take it from me - I\u2019m just a guy messing around at home in my free time. There are already many cool FROs and BBNs doing cool work outside of academia!</p><p>And so people outside of academia should be able to at least <em><strong>ask</strong></em> for grant funding. </p><p>So that\u2019s why, on behalf of The Independent Science Society, we are undersigning Science Works\u2019 letter on Reforming UKRI Eligibility. The letter is <a href=\"https://science.works/writing/open-letter-reforming-ukri-eligibility/\">here</a>. It argues that the eligibility rules make it impossible for new orgs to ask for money, and the main ask is as quoted</p><blockquote><p>First, <strong>UKRI should remove the de facto ban on supporting new organisations. It should achieve this by offering a forward-looking route through which new organisations can demonstrate research capability and financial viability. Significant financial support from funders that UKRI already trusts should provide such a route.</strong> To that end, UKRI should publish a list of trusted funders, including at a minimum those on the existing list of endorsed funders, and should update it regularly.</p><p>Second, <strong>UKRI should remove the artificial distinction between standard and non-standard eligibility.</strong> The requirements for standard eligibility are practically identical to those for the highest band of non-standard eligibility, yet organisations meeting these materially equivalent criteria are treated differently. This distinction blocks organisations with non-standard eligibility from accessing support, even when they have been deemed to have sufficient research capability and appropriate financial governance. <strong>If non-standard eligibility must be kept, UKRI\u2019s Executive Committee should mandate all calls to be open by default to organisations with either type of eligibility.</strong></p></blockquote><p>I encourage you to click and check it out. Here is a screenshot of the beginning, and please read it in full.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JkTp!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4016a2af-6ce1-4344-b6be-0a7c4397572d_744x465.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JkTp!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4016a2af-6ce1-4344-b6be-0a7c4397572d_744x465.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JkTp!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4016a2af-6ce1-4344-b6be-0a7c4397572d_744x465.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JkTp!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4016a2af-6ce1-4344-b6be-0a7c4397572d_744x465.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JkTp!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressi